[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: One stdlib HTTP server serves the app over the resident daemon

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SDOC-BOARD-SERVER
TITLE: One stdlib HTTP server serves the app over the resident daemon
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
server.py is one stdlib threaded HTTP server with an allowlisted static surface and three JSON routes: /api/health, /api/graph, and /api/rows. source.py obtains workspace.describe, workspace.export, and workspace.grammar from the resident daemon, validates the grammar reply, adapts all payloads, and caches them by daemon generation. Repeat requests do not re-export an unchanged workspace. NoDaemon becomes HTTP 503 with the daemon start remedy; other daemon failures become 502.

R7 separately pins the board interpreter with Pydantic. Until that commit is combined, source.py uses the shared WorkspaceGrammarResult model when it is importable and an exact, fail-closed shape validator otherwise; the shared-understanding debt node records removal of that compatibility branch. Semantics construction still reads the operator-owned semantics model from disk. The source labels that path as a recorded violation of REQ-DAEMON-IS-THE-ONLY-SOURCE rather than disguising it as daemon data.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Updated 2026-09-03 for commits 8823edf1 and 46cd3cf1: the static allowlist
grew grammar-groups.json and fsm.js, and source.py gained the semantics
payload. The three JSON routes are unchanged -- semantics rides inside
/api/graph rather than on a fourth route.

Updated 2026-09-08 for commit 8b936c3c: the allowlist grew two more entries,
/assets/vendor/elkjs/elk-api.js and /assets/vendor/elkjs/elk-worker.min.js,
and they are the only ones not backed by a file in this directory -- server.py
resolves them against the Nix store path in SDOC_BOARD_ELKJS_DIR and refuses
to start when that variable is unset or does not hold both files. So the
process now asks one thing of its environment beyond a python3;
MECH-SDOC-BOARD-LAYOUT owns the delivery. Still three JSON routes.
<<<
